WEBVTT

00:26.930 --> 00:29.710
Did you hear what happened to Kaibara?

00:29.710 --> 00:32.550
Apparently, his conquest of Grün failed.

00:33.370 --> 00:38.900
On top of that, Sengoku is 
struggling in the desert.

00:40.840 --> 00:43.970
Dwarven strongholds are known for 
being impregnable, after all.

00:44.450 --> 00:50.810
It seems we underestimated 
their ally from Hellsehen.

00:51.580 --> 00:54.240
The Wizard of Hurricanes, huh?

00:54.240 --> 00:57.010
He's a more difficult 
opponent than expected.

01:13.680 --> 01:15.260
Aw, I'm out.

01:15.260 --> 01:17.830
Hey, what are you drinking for?!

01:18.630 --> 01:20.470
We're at war!

01:20.470 --> 01:22.800
Now, now. Calm down.

01:23.470 --> 01:27.280
You worry too much, Little Miss Ysha.

01:29.160 --> 01:31.990
This is hardly appropriate behavior 
for the commander of a nation!

01:31.990 --> 01:35.150
That's just what people decided to call me.

01:35.150 --> 01:36.960
I'm just a priest.

01:40.200 --> 01:45.210
Are you planning to attack soon, 
Fallen Angel of Misery?

01:48.960 --> 01:49.920
Not good!

01:49.920 --> 01:51.660
Do something, Wolff!

01:51.660 --> 01:54.620
As you wish, Ysha.

01:54.950 --> 01:57.070
Hey, Doran!

01:57.070 --> 02:00.590
Could you draw their forces to the east side?

02:00.590 --> 02:02.910
Shut your mouth, whelp!

02:02.910 --> 02:05.490
I'm not obeying your orders!

02:06.260 --> 02:08.950
Just sit there quietly and watch!

02:13.450 --> 02:20.040
If you want the head of the courageous 
General Doran, then follow me, lizards!

02:18.070 --> 02:20.030
<b>King of Gelb
Doran</b>

02:24.270 --> 02:27.020
Not very honest, is he?

02:27.800 --> 02:29.970
That's it. There will do.

02:29.970 --> 02:31.870
What are you...

02:31.870 --> 02:33.420
Stand back, Little Miss Ysha.

02:35.650 --> 02:38.760
Scythe of dancing wind spirits...

02:41.720 --> 02:43.970
Sturm und Drang!

03:04.750 --> 03:07.960
Look! The enemy forces are retreating!

03:09.310 --> 03:11.390
There's no need to give chase.

03:11.390 --> 03:13.180
We should withdraw, as well.

03:13.670 --> 03:15.420
Th-That's...

03:20.320 --> 03:22.330
S-Sensei?!

03:21.200 --> 03:24.180
Oh, crap! I hit a citizen!

03:24.180 --> 03:24.930
Actually, wait...

03:24.930 --> 03:26.740
You know him?!

04:51.900 --> 04:55.400
<b>No Longer Allowed               in Another World</b>

04:55.400 --> 04:56.700
<b>[ No Longer Allowed               in Another World ]</b>

04:56.700 --> 04:59.950
<b>[ No Longer Allowed               in Another World ]</b>

05:07.700 --> 05:12.370
The forces of the Seven Fallen 
Angels are nothing to fear!

05:12.660 --> 05:16.620
The church is responsible for the 
Fallen Other Worlder problem, anyway!

05:16.870 --> 05:22.380
They should be thanking us for 
cleaning up their mess for them!

05:22.380 --> 05:23.340
Yeah!

05:23.340 --> 05:25.300
You tell 'em, King Doran!

05:25.300 --> 05:26.800
Now, now.

05:27.380 --> 05:31.430
That's enough trash-talking my boss.

05:32.180 --> 05:35.640
Sounds like something one of his 
loyal dogs would say, Wolff.

05:35.640 --> 05:38.520
He's got a lot on his plate.

05:38.520 --> 05:43.570
That said, we're driving off the 
Fallen Angels without his help.

05:43.570 --> 05:45.110
Isn't that enough?

05:45.440 --> 05:49.660
It's thanks to the incredible 
effort of you dwarves.

05:50.200 --> 05:53.040
I appreciate it, Doran.

05:54.120 --> 05:59.210
You've been doing a decent 
job, for a weakling elf.

05:59.210 --> 06:01.840
I suppose you deserve some praise.

06:02.880 --> 06:04.630
You honor me.

06:06.760 --> 06:09.590
Drink up, boys!

06:09.590 --> 06:11.970
More battle awaits us tomorrow!

06:18.270 --> 06:20.100
So good!

06:22.900 --> 06:26.490
I wasn't expecting to 
run into you again here.

06:26.490 --> 06:28.580
We've been through a lot.

06:28.860 --> 06:31.740
We got lost in the vast desert,

06:31.740 --> 06:35.200
and before we knew it, Sensei 
had been caught in a tornado.

06:35.200 --> 06:37.370
Oh, right. How is Sensei?

06:37.370 --> 06:38.660
He's fine now.

06:39.040 --> 06:41.960
We were fortunate that 
he was inside his cof—

06:41.960 --> 06:43.630
What was fortunate?

06:44.130 --> 06:47.240
It was unfortunate that 
I was inside my coffin.

06:47.630 --> 06:51.090
Because of that, I survived again.

06:51.090 --> 06:53.220
I see you haven't changed, Sensei.

06:55.060 --> 06:58.060
And now my precious bed has been broken.

06:59.600 --> 07:02.690
I'll buy you a new coffin soon.

07:02.690 --> 07:04.020
You pay for everything, huh?

07:04.440 --> 07:07.280
Good to see you again, Bishop Annette.

07:07.280 --> 07:08.240
Wolff.

07:08.240 --> 07:10.820
Rather, former Bishop Annette.

07:19.830 --> 07:22.210
How are you feeling?

07:22.670 --> 07:24.840
Sorry for accidentally hitting you, too.

07:25.210 --> 07:30.510
You should reflect on your 
failure to kill me properly.

07:30.510 --> 07:31.300
Huh?

07:32.090 --> 07:33.140
That said,

07:33.640 --> 07:37.180
I did get to try a new near-death experience.

07:37.180 --> 07:38.850
Thank you for that.

07:38.850 --> 07:41.600
You're a strange man, aren't you?

07:42.940 --> 07:46.900
I hope you'll overlook this as 
a mistake made during war.

07:46.900 --> 07:48.110
War?

07:48.110 --> 07:50.400
Right, you don't know.

07:50.940 --> 07:55.910
This nation is currently at war with 
one of the Seven Fallen Angels.

07:56.660 --> 07:58.360
Seven Fallen Angels?

07:58.660 --> 08:03.040
I already defeated one of those in Grün!

08:03.040 --> 08:04.170
You did what?!

08:04.880 --> 08:06.210
You did, missy?

08:06.590 --> 08:09.210
There must be some mistake.

08:09.210 --> 08:12.400
Or perhaps he was very weak.

08:12.400 --> 08:13.720
What did you say?!

08:13.720 --> 08:15.090
Now, now.

08:15.090 --> 08:16.930
Don't underestimate us.

08:16.930 --> 08:19.680
Our party's pretty strong.

08:19.970 --> 08:24.350
Why, Sensei has the ability to send 
Fallen Other Worlders elsewhere!

08:24.350 --> 08:26.770
So I've heard from Little Miss Ysha.

08:27.560 --> 08:31.650
The pope expresses interest 
in his ability, as well.

08:33.650 --> 08:39.990
But I don't think we need that power.

08:39.990 --> 08:41.000
What?

08:41.000 --> 08:43.910
No matter what kind of Gift 
someone shows up with,

08:44.210 --> 08:48.630
it's meaningless in the face of my magic.

08:51.420 --> 08:53.470
Wolff, you've had too much to drink.

08:56.890 --> 09:00.470
In any case, we'll handle 
the Seven Fallen Angels.

09:04.810 --> 09:09.400
You be good and sit tight, 
our alleged savior.

09:11.390 --> 09:13.940
What a jerk.

09:13.940 --> 09:15.990
Is he really that impressive?

09:15.990 --> 09:19.120
Yes. That's Wolff, the Wizard of Storms.

09:19.450 --> 09:23.830
Without a doubt, he is one of the 
strongest wizards in the world.

09:24.120 --> 09:30.590
Even the Seven Fallen Angels are powerless 
against his magic and intellect.

09:37.090 --> 09:38.840
Welcome back.

09:38.840 --> 09:42.300
I never thought you'd be forced to retreat.

09:42.300 --> 09:43.810
It's not a problem.

09:43.810 --> 09:46.480
Tomorrow, I will join the battle.

09:46.890 --> 09:49.440
We will not be beaten again.

09:49.440 --> 09:55.110
Actually, I was thinking of changing our 
tack and having the women handle this.

09:58.320 --> 10:04.660
I've sent someone who knows the 
Wizard of Storms well to the desert.

10:11.420 --> 10:13.210
Are you ready,

10:14.920 --> 10:17.050
Fallen Angel of Greed?

10:22.480 --> 10:26.360
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:22.980 --> 10:26.360
Reflect on Your
Failure to Kill
Me Properly

10:26.360 --> 10:27.240
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:26.400 --> 10:27.200
Reflect on Your
Failure to Kill
Me Properly

10:27.200 --> 10:27.240
Reflect on Your
Failure to Kill
Me Properly

10:27.240 --> 10:27.280
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:27.240 --> 10:27.280
Reflect on Your
Failure to Kill
Me Properly

10:27.320 --> 10:27.320
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:27.320 --> 10:27.410
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:27.410 --> 10:27.450
<b>No Longer Allowed in Another World</b>

10:33.940 --> 10:36.650
Why the long face?

10:38.030 --> 10:41.370
I see. You're lovesick, aren't you?

10:41.820 --> 10:44.280
You miss that girl we met earlier, don't you?

10:45.330 --> 10:50.540
A one-sided love is the greatest kind of love.

10:50.540 --> 10:53.130
You should enjoy your anguish.

10:53.790 --> 10:55.750
Ow, ow, ow.

11:02.760 --> 11:07.140
Very well, Melos. We'll look for her together.

11:08.930 --> 11:11.690
Come to think of it, you and I are the same.

11:12.650 --> 11:19.030
We're foolish men wandering 
this world in search of a woman.

11:19.820 --> 11:23.530
By the way, what should 
we call your beloved?

11:23.990 --> 11:27.490
Since she's a female version 
of you, how about Femmelos?

11:31.080 --> 11:32.790
You seem to like it.

11:33.920 --> 11:36.590
Speak of the devil.

11:42.010 --> 11:44.140
You look gorgeous again today, Mr. Wolff!

11:44.140 --> 11:47.010
You're going drinking, right? 
We'll join you all night long!

11:47.010 --> 11:49.180
Sorry, but not today.

11:49.180 --> 11:50.230
Aw!

11:50.890 --> 11:54.440
Her master seems quite 
popular with the ladies.

11:56.570 --> 11:59.190
He's the opposite of you, Melos.

12:00.900 --> 12:02.530
Don't let it get you down.

12:04.070 --> 12:09.790
A man simply ought to pursue a 
woman until she looks his way.

12:25.550 --> 12:27.680
It's me. Open up.

12:30.680 --> 12:32.810
She won't see me again today.

12:33.850 --> 12:35.940
Now, this is a surprise.

12:35.940 --> 12:38.730
Melos, he's like you.

12:39.940 --> 12:44.950
Even that playboy is 
pursuing his own beloved.

12:46.780 --> 12:49.900
In that case, just listen.

12:50.410 --> 12:55.670
The war is ongoing, but I promise 
I'll come back alive.

12:56.630 --> 13:01.050
When I do, this time, I'll...

13:01.760 --> 13:03.470
Let's go, Melos.

13:04.680 --> 13:08.550
It would be petty of us to stay any longer.

13:14.230 --> 13:15.360
I bring news!

13:15.730 --> 13:18.900
Enemy forces are attacking 
from the East Gelb Dunes!

13:18.900 --> 13:20.320
They're here.

13:20.320 --> 13:21.610
We'll fight, too.

13:21.610 --> 13:23.070
You're our guests. Stay here and relax.

13:23.070 --> 13:26.780
I'm off to put a little hurt 
on the Seven Fallen Angels.

13:28.280 --> 13:32.610
Today we'll defeat the Fallen 
Angel of Misery and end this war!

13:32.920 --> 13:35.160
Let's go, boys!

13:50.800 --> 13:53.430
Thanks, priest! You saved us!

13:53.430 --> 13:56.440
This area is secure! 
Go reinforce undermanned areas!

13:56.440 --> 13:57.310
Got it!

13:57.690 --> 14:01.180
Good. We're crushing them.

14:01.180 --> 14:02.640
Wolff, look to the west.

14:04.740 --> 14:06.200
Something is coming.

14:27.280 --> 14:30.340
Damn it! No one said 
anything about a dragon!

14:32.310 --> 14:35.020
That's Jade the Dark Dragon!

14:35.020 --> 14:38.060
A legendary dragon that was once 
under the Dark Lord's command!

14:38.060 --> 14:40.560
And now it's their pawn.

14:40.560 --> 14:42.270
Poor thing.

14:42.270 --> 14:43.900
I'm disappointed, though.

14:44.400 --> 14:48.700
That's your ace in the hole, 
Fallen Angel of Misery?

14:49.490 --> 14:53.580
I've taken down dozens of dragons before.

14:55.490 --> 14:56.540
Huh?

14:59.500 --> 15:00.790
Hey, Wolff!

15:00.790 --> 15:04.250
That's not the Fallen Angel 
of Misery riding the dragon!

15:04.250 --> 15:05.800
So what?

15:05.800 --> 15:09.760
No matter who they are, I'll rip 
them to shreds with my magic!

15:13.300 --> 15:14.420
They're coming!

15:22.190 --> 15:23.060
Huh?!

15:29.450 --> 15:32.740
It's good to see you again, Master.

15:33.320 --> 15:35.410
Why are you...

15:38.700 --> 15:40.370
What is it, Wolff?

15:46.840 --> 15:47.760
Wolff!

15:48.210 --> 15:49.630
You fiend!

15:52.090 --> 15:55.300
<i>Wh-What is this? I feel weak...</i>

15:56.350 --> 15:57.560
Don't worry.

15:58.140 --> 16:03.060
I promise I'll kill you later, too.

16:04.560 --> 16:07.070
I just have business with him first.

16:12.860 --> 16:14.200
Wolff!

16:17.200 --> 16:20.160
Hey! What's happening up there?!

16:22.290 --> 16:23.870
Retreat...

16:24.330 --> 16:27.340
You must retreat, King Doran!

16:27.340 --> 16:28.750
What?!

16:31.050 --> 16:33.760
Bishop Wolff? No...

16:33.760 --> 16:37.050
They took Wolff and flew southwest.

16:37.050 --> 16:40.180
They probably headed towards Dritten Temple.

16:40.810 --> 16:44.350
<i>That woman called Wolff "Master."</i>

16:44.690 --> 16:46.440
<i>Who is she?</i>

16:48.320 --> 16:51.780
Our forces are in chaos, 
and the lizards are pressing in.

16:51.780 --> 16:56.060
Relying on that whelp caught up to us.

16:56.060 --> 16:58.830
At this rate, the castle will fall.

17:00.950 --> 17:02.290
Look, Melos.

17:02.830 --> 17:06.580
Femmelos's heart is broken 
because her master is in danger.

17:07.000 --> 17:11.380
What should a man do when 
he sees a woman cry?

17:11.670 --> 17:14.840
You know the answer to 
that, don't you, Melos?

17:24.270 --> 17:25.440
Good boy.

17:27.100 --> 17:31.900
It seems to me Wolff-kun 
has a complicated past.

17:32.530 --> 17:36.910
Perhaps his beloved knows something.

17:41.990 --> 17:43.950
Who is it?

17:43.950 --> 17:46.290
Forgive the sudden visit, miss.

17:46.790 --> 17:50.290
May I ask you a few questions about Wolff?

18:02.890 --> 18:06.190
I see. Now this is very interesting.

18:14.820 --> 18:17.400
You're awake, Master.

18:19.070 --> 18:20.820
Dritten Temple...

18:21.780 --> 18:24.040
A memorable place for us both.

18:25.160 --> 18:28.670
The place of my youth.

18:32.380 --> 18:33.670
Yuriko...

18:33.960 --> 18:35.220
Bishop Wolff!

18:36.090 --> 18:39.390
Who are you?! Release the bishop!

18:40.550 --> 18:46.350
Because of you, Master, 
my abilities have finally blossomed.

18:48.520 --> 18:50.310
Stay out of my way.

18:51.690 --> 18:54.890
That woman may be Wolff's student.

18:55.360 --> 19:00.280
He was once more passionate than 
anyone about training Other Worlders.

19:00.700 --> 19:05.860
But he suddenly stopped one day and 
began drowning himself in drink.

19:06.330 --> 19:08.960
Was that student the cause?

19:08.960 --> 19:10.500
I don't know.

19:10.500 --> 19:13.880
Either way, rescuing Wolff 
is our top priority.

19:13.880 --> 19:15.800
King Doran, send soldiers right away.

19:15.800 --> 19:18.550
I wish I could,

19:18.550 --> 19:21.640
but I don't have soldiers to spare.

19:24.100 --> 19:27.390
Oh, fine.

19:27.390 --> 19:31.440
Since we defeated one of the Seven 
Fallen Angels, we'll take the job.

19:31.730 --> 19:35.980
I'm sure it was God who brought us here.

19:35.980 --> 19:37.400
You lot...

19:37.400 --> 19:39.290
Right, Sensei?

19:39.610 --> 19:41.450
Huh? Where's Sensei?

19:41.910 --> 19:44.780
Come to think of it, he wasn't 
here last night, either.

19:45.910 --> 19:47.750
I'm right here.

19:52.370 --> 19:55.040
Don't mind us. Continue your conversation.

19:55.040 --> 19:56.450
How can we not mind?!

19:56.450 --> 19:59.720
Why is he always finding new women?!

19:59.720 --> 20:00.410
Now, now.

20:00.410 --> 20:03.180
Do adults not care who they're with?

20:03.180 --> 20:05.600
Look! You're a terrible 
influence on children!

20:04.890 --> 20:06.930
There is no God...

20:06.930 --> 20:10.140
We are still at war, you know.

20:12.140 --> 20:13.170
Now, then...

20:15.980 --> 20:18.530
Let's go.

20:18.940 --> 20:21.570
I'm sorry this is all we can do for you.

20:21.570 --> 20:24.780
You gave us new equipment for free. 
I have nothing to complain about.

20:24.780 --> 20:28.290
That's right. The nation of craftsmen 
never fails to impress. These are great.

20:28.290 --> 20:30.040
One moment, please.

20:30.330 --> 20:33.000
The item I requested has not arrived yet.

20:33.370 --> 20:35.960
What? You need equipment, Sensei?

20:35.960 --> 20:38.460
He's carrying that old woman again...

20:38.460 --> 20:43.430
The item you requested is too specialized. 
The craftsmen are confused.

20:43.430 --> 20:45.840
They haven't finished it yet.

20:45.840 --> 20:46.800
Honestly...

20:47.390 --> 20:50.390
And you call yourselves 
a nation of craftsmen.

20:50.390 --> 20:52.180
I've had it with this guy.

20:53.310 --> 20:56.020
In any case, we must hurry. 
Wolff's life is in danger.

20:56.020 --> 20:58.320
But we're supposed to cross this?

20:58.320 --> 21:00.030
We'll be exhausted by 
the time we get there.

21:00.030 --> 21:01.990
You need some help?

21:06.560 --> 21:09.240
Toru the Huntsman has arrived!

21:09.240 --> 21:11.410
Good to see your faces again!

21:11.410 --> 21:13.620
Oh, come on! We're in a hurry!

21:13.620 --> 21:17.080
Wait, wait! I'm not here to fight!

21:17.080 --> 21:20.500
I've mended my ways since 
Boss Nir saved my life!

21:20.500 --> 21:21.700
"Boss"?

21:21.700 --> 21:26.770
Now I run a bus company by day and 
guard the orphanage by night!

21:22.820 --> 21:26.760
Huntsmen's

21:26.770 --> 21:29.390
Oh, you're protecting the orphanage, huh?

21:29.390 --> 21:31.480
So... what's a "bus"?

21:31.820 --> 21:34.680
Huh? Okay, just watch this!

21:35.010 --> 21:38.560
Overpowered Skill: Lucifer's Hammer!

21:38.560 --> 21:41.820
Anything I use my skill on...

21:43.930 --> 21:46.100
turns into a vehicle!

21:46.110 --> 21:46.660
<b>Gelb Castle</b>

21:46.740 --> 21:48.070
<b>Dritten Temple</b>

21:47.360 --> 21:49.770
Hop in, everyone!

21:49.770 --> 21:52.030
Wow!

21:56.000 --> 21:56.970
What?

21:56.970 --> 21:59.320
I'm not letting you on!

21:59.320 --> 22:03.040
Go mourn Chavez until the 
49th day after his death!

22:03.040 --> 22:04.620
Huh? Wait! Sensei!

22:04.620 --> 22:07.760
Now, let's go!

22:07.760 --> 22:09.610
Hey! What are you doing?!

22:09.610 --> 22:11.130
Please turn back!

22:11.130 --> 22:15.090
The words "turn back" aren't 
found in my dictionary!

22:13.660 --> 22:15.090
Hey!

22:19.300 --> 22:21.550
I guess I'll head back.

22:25.820 --> 22:28.910
<b>m 0 0 l 160 0 160 40 0 40</b>

22:25.820 --> 22:28.910
<b>Sensei gazes intently at
the coffin fragment.</b>

22:25.830 --> 22:28.540
You're the only vehicle for me.

22:31.140 --> 22:33.200
Quiet, Melos.

22:33.660 --> 22:38.510
I know you want Femmelos's attention, 
but there's nothing to be done about it now.

22:38.970 --> 22:43.550
Besides, Wolff-kun told me 
to be good and sit ti—

22:45.020 --> 22:49.890
Please take me with you to Mr. Wolff.

22:49.890 --> 22:54.340
Now, this is a surprise. 
You've been quiet until now.

22:55.410 --> 22:57.310
I...

22:57.800 --> 23:00.560
I must go to him.

23:07.370 --> 23:09.650
Ow, ow, ow.

23:10.760 --> 23:12.480
Good grief.

23:12.480 --> 23:18.950
I've had enough of the obsession of 
those pursuing the ones they love.

23:19.380 --> 23:24.700
You cast aside reason and common sense, 
caring not if you inconvenience others.

23:26.130 --> 23:32.130
But that is what makes it the 
seed of a beautiful story.

23:35.270 --> 23:38.740
Shall we go, miss?
